## Findings and defaults

1. TypeScript `7.0.2` is the only stable 7.0.x. `latest` is `7.0.2`.
2. The live scan finds 43 workspaces with `check-types` (and 47 with `test`). The plan says 31. Twelve workspaces joined
   after Phase 1. Default: run all of them and check the 31 by name. The TR2 "Done when" line in `plan.md` changed.
3. The 5.9.3 control runs inside TR4. The install state flips 5.9.3, 7.0.x, 5.9.3, 7.0.x. TR1 ends on 7.0.x as the plan asks.
4. Control tests run only for workspaces that fail under 7.0.x. `improved` applies to type checks only.
5. TR5 fixes ship as patch files in the evidence folder and do not land on master in Phase 3. TR8 removes the branch
   with `git branch -D` after every commit has a patch.
6. `phase1-pre-existing-failures.json` has no row that maps to a type-check or test result of a workspace. The decision
   "pre-existing" uses the 5.9.3 control on the same tree, and cites `compiler-baseline.json` when it has an entry.
7. The five stale Phase 2 test names in section 5b.10 are an inference from the cause text in `plan.md`. The orchestrator
   observes the names at `phase_base_sha`. The observed set wins.
8. The `spec.md` "Time window" bullet now says the window is lifted (PM 2026-11-28), in one line.
9. The package `typescript@7.0.2` has no classic JS compiler API in its root export. Expect `js-api-consumer` regressions
   for `tsup`, `ts-node`, and `typescript-eslint`. TR7 probes this.

